1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,360
This demonstration shows the Explainable AI Email Triage application
operating as a controlled local research prototype.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:11,840
The system is designed to support human review of potentially urgent
email.

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:18,160
It does not make an autonomous routing decision, and it is not approved
for shadow testing or production deployment.

4
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:22,770
The notice at the top of the application states the most important
boundary.

5
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:27,730
The current model disposition is revise, and every result requires human
review.

6
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:36,210
Gate A passed because the software workflow can load the verified local
artifact, accept a bounded input, return a repeatable result, and fail
safely.

7
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:41,730
That engineering result does not mean the classifier has passed the
separate predictive-reliability gate.

8
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,020
For this demonstration, I am using a fully synthetic message.

9
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:52,100
The subject is “Synthetic deadline reminder,” and the body asks for
review before 3 PM today.

10
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:57,220
No private email, reviewer note, address, or other personal information
is being entered.

11
00:00:58,070 --> 00:00:59,590
I will select Analyze.

12
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:04,790
The model returns an urgency probability of approximately 49.5 percent.

13
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:09,430
At the 0.45 threshold, the message is classified as urgent.

14
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:14,470
At the 0.50 threshold, the same message is classified as nonurgent.

15
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:18,790
This disagreement is the main finding the interface is designed to make
visible.

16
00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:27,270
A small threshold change alters the classification, so the application
does not hide that uncertainty or choose an operating threshold for the
user.

17
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:34,920
The next section shows features that supported the urgent and nonurgent
sides of the fitted logistic-regression calculation.

18
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:38,680
These contributions help explain how this model produced the score.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,720
They are not causal explanations, and they do not prove why a message is
truly urgent.

20
00:01:44,570 --> 00:01:48,330
The required-handling card keeps a person in the decision process.

21
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:54,810
The result remains marked revise, the input-retention field says no, and
deployment approval remains no.

22
00:01:55,130 --> 00:02:01,450
The application returns a research result for review, but it does not
route the message or save the submitted subject and body.

23
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:05,820
The validated workflow also includes safe failure behavior.

24
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:10,860
This second local instance was intentionally started with a model path
that does not exist.

25
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:15,980
Its health response reports not ready and explains that the local
research artifact was not found.

26
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:21,500
The disposition remains revise, and deployment and shadow-testing
approval remain false.

27
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:29,180
If an analysis is requested in this condition, the service returns an
unavailable response instead of loading a different model or fabricating
a prediction.

28
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:36,140
I used a separate path and port for this check, so the verified model
artifact was not deleted, renamed, or altered.

29
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:40,830
Before preparing this recording, I reran the documented validation.

30
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:43,710
All 13 automated tests passed.

31
00:02:44,030 --> 00:02:54,750
The validator also completed 60 deterministic synthetic inference runs
and confirmed visible thresholds, bounded explanations, privacy-safe
output, and the research-only artifact boundary.

32
00:02:55,600 --> 00:03:00,240
This demonstration satisfies the Week 8 requirement to show the AI model
in action.

33
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:04,000
It also preserves the evidence boundary established during the project.

34
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:17,200
The software is ready for a repeatable local demonstration, while the
classifier still needs more labeled data, a newly reserved untouched
test set, and stronger reliability evidence before any operational
recommendation should be considered.

35
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:24,610
For anyone reviewing the evidence, the best place to start is the
Project Review Guide linked from the repository's main README.

36
00:03:24,930 --> 00:03:31,090
The guide connects the written conclusions in the docs folder to the
exact CSV and JSON evidence in the results folder.

37
00:03:31,410 --> 00:03:41,650
The Week 6 experiment record supports the threshold findings, while the
Week 7 automated test report and demo validation file support the
13-test and 60-inference results.

38
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:47,330
The demonstration runbook explains how to reproduce the application and
safe-failure check.

39
00:03:47,650 --> 00:03:53,650
This structure makes each statement in the demonstration traceable
without requiring the reviewer to search through the repository.

40
00:03:54,500 --> 00:04:00,180
Thank you, Professor, and thank you to everyone in the class for your
time, feedback, and support throughout this project.

41
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,860
I appreciate the opportunity to share the final demonstration.
